### Programming Problem
Given a large list of numbers, design a data structure that supports efficient insertion, deletion, and retrieval of the k-th smallest element. Implement a function `kth_smallest` that returns the k-th smallest element from the data structure after a series of insertions and deletions.

### Reasoning
1. The problem now requires supporting additional operations (retrieval of the k-th smallest element).
2. A balanced binary search tree (BST), such as an AVL tree or a Red-Black tree, can efficiently support these operations with O(log n) time complexity.
3. We will implement an AVL tree to maintain balance and support the required operations.

### Pseudo-code
