2. Add a flag to detect if any swaps were made during a pass through the array. If no swaps are made, the array is already sorted, and the algorithm can terminate early.
3. Modify the loop to include the swap counting and early termination logic.

Pseudo-code:
```
function bubbleSortWithCount(arr):
    n = length(arr)
    swap_count = 0
    for i from 0 to n-1:
        swapped = false
        for j from 1 to n-i-1:
            if arr[j-1] > arr[j]:
                swap(arr[j-1], arr[j])
                swap_count = swap_count + 1
                swapped = true
        if not swapped:
            break
    return swap_count
```

Final Code:
public class BubbleSortEnhanced {
    public static int bubbleSort(int[] arr) {
        int n = arr.length;
        int swapCount = 0;
        boolean swapped;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            swapped = false;
            for (int j = 1; j < (n - i); j++) {
                if (arr[j - 1] > arr[j]) {
                    int temp = arr[j - 1];
                    arr[j - 1] = arr[j];
                    arr[j] = temp;
                    swapCount++;
                    swapped = true;
                }
            }
            if (!swapped) {
                break;
            }
        }
        return swapCount;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] array = {4, 3, 5, 2, 1};
        int swaps = bubbleSort(array);
        System.out.println("Sorted Array: ");
        for (int num : array) {
            System.out.print(num + " ");
        }
        System.out.println("\nNumber of Swaps: " + swaps);
    }
}

